<td><ul>
<li>Parameter or Variable: BATHYMETRY (measured); Units: meter; Observation Category: in situ; Sampling Instrument: multibeam sonar; Sampling and Analyzing Method: Acoustic water column data was collected aboard the NOAA Ship Nancy Foster using a hull mounted Reson 7125 mulitbeam system. All acoustic samples were georeferenced using Applanix POS MV 320 version 5 GNSS inertial positioning system. The survey was conducted in a grid pattern and the data (.s7k format) was organized by date and location for post processing; Data Quality Method: Post Processing Steps 1.) Reson 7125 (.s7k) data files were processed using Echoview Software Package Version 10.0.255. Fish Targets were detected using a multibeam target detection algorithm that creates from groups of adjoining data points. The resulting target has a range and major-axis angle corresponding to the geometric center of the group. The data target were exported for analysis in RStudio Version 3.5. 2.) R Statistical Software was used to calculate to calculate the position of each target (latitude, longitude, and depth) and the resulting georeferenced targets were exported as an ESRI ArcGIS shape file. 3.) The georeferenced shape files that were created in R Studio (previous step) are imported into an ESRI ArcGIS Pro 2.4.0 file geodatabase using the ‘Feature to 3D by Attribute’ geoprocessing tool within the ‘3D Analyst’ toolbox and set to the appropriate 3D Symbology where white spheres represent fish targets. Sphere size is standard and does not vary by attribute. Fish target depth is represented in the z-dimension. These fish targets from wide-angle multibeam convey the extent of fish schools that were detected as a smaller slice with the narrow-beam angle split beam echo sounder. Data were projected in WGS 1984 Web Mercator Auxiliary Sphere (ESPG: 3857). The geodatabase was exported to a web layer to the online shipwreck atlas service hosted by ESRI ArcGIS.</li>
<li>Parameter or Variable: Acoustic Backscatter (measured); Units: n/a; Observation Category: in situ; Sampling Instrument: Split Beam Sonar; Sampling and Analyzing Method: Acoustic water column data was collected aboard the NOAA Ship Nancy Foster using a hull mounted Simrad 120kHz transducer scientific echo sounder. All acoustic samples were georeferenced using Applanix POS MV 320 version 5 GNSS inertial positioning system. The Simrad echo sounder was calibrated in the field with a tungsten carbide sphere based on factory specifications. The survey was conducted in a grid pattern and the data (.raw format) was organized by date and location for post processing.; Data Quality Method: Data collection parameters: EK60SaCorrection -0.7038dB Ek60TransducerGain 25.6700dB Frequency 120.00 kHz MajorAxis3dbBeamAngle 6.73º MajorAxisAngleOffset -0.05º MajorAxisAngleSensitivity 23.000000 MinorAxis3dbBeamAngle 6.84º MinorAxisAngleOffset 0.03º MinorAxisAngleSensitivity 23.000000 SoundSpeed 1547.66m/s TransmittedPower 250.00000W TransmittedPulseLength 0.128ms TvgRangeCorrection SimradEx60 TwoWayBeamAngle -20.400000dB re 1sr</li>
</ul></td>
</tr>
